#!RuleTest
#test PMDA-CT2003 expect=noViolation domain=LB
#note "The negative half of the '#library codelist-codes' contract, and the probe that proves the directive is load-bearing: byte-identical data to the invalid twin (ALB against the decode Bilirubin) but with no codelist-codes declared, so getCodelistCodeMap is empty, the accessor returns NO DECISION for every row and the rule reports nothing. Note the verdict is noViolation, not skipped: the accessor's LIBRARY gate trips on a NULL provider only, and the fda/pmda families require '#library standard=...' on every scenario, so the provider is always present here."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 0
dataset LB label="Laboratory Test Results"
col STUDYID  type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN   type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID  type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col LBTESTCD type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Short Name"
col LBTEST   type=Char label="Lab Test or Examination Name"
---
S1 | LB | 001 | ALB | Albumin
S1 | LB | 002 | ALB | Bilirubin
